        "298:298": {"phenotype": "Softer texture", "cell_wall": "Increased degradation", "softening": "Faster"}
      },
      "notes": "SSR marker targeting the Md-PG1 gene encoding polygalacturonase, an enzyme responsible for cell wall breakdown during ripening. The 10kDa SSR region shows significant allelic diversity.",
